{"strongs": "H3076", "word": "יְהוֺחָנָן", "translit": "ye.ho.cha.nan", "root": "הוד", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "hath been gracious", "definition": "יְהוֺחָנָן , יוֺחָנָן proper name, masculine ᵐ5 mostly Ἰωαναν , Ἰωναν ( ׳ י hath been gracious , compare אֶלְחָנָן חֲנַנְאֵל & references; also Phoenician יחנבעל בעליחן ) — 1. a. ׳ יְהוֺ a priest Neh 12:13 \\ \\ b. high priest Ezra 10:6 = יוֺחָנָן Neh 12:22 ; Neh 12:23 apparently = יוֺנָתָן Neh 12:11 (twice in verse) ( ᵐ5 Ἰωναθαν ). 2. ׳ יְהוֺ Levite Neh 12:42 . 3. ׳ יְהוֺ son of Tobiah Neh 6:18 ( ᵐ5 Manuscripts Ἰωναθαν ). 4. ׳ יְהוֺ porter in David's time 1Chr 26:3 ( ᵐ5 Ἰωνας , ᵐ5 L Ἰωναθαν ). 5. ׳ יְהוֺ a Judaite captain 2Chr 17:15 apparently also 2Chr 23:1 . 6. ׳ יְהוֺ an Ephraimite 2Chr 28:12 . 7. ׳ יְהוֺ an Israelite, Ezra's time Ezra 10:28 . 8. ׳ יוֺ (& so all following) a Jewish captain, after fall of Jerusalem 2Kgs 25:23 ; Jer 40:8 ; Jer 40:13 ; Jer 40:15 ; Jer 40:16 ; Jer 41:11 ; Jer 41:13 ; Jer 41:14 ; Jer 41:15 ; Jer 41:16 ; Jer 42:1 ; Jer 42:8 ; Jer 43:2 ; Jer 43:4 ; Jer 43:5 9. eldest son of king Josiah 1Chr 3:15 ᵐ5 L Ἰωαχας (apparently = יְתוֺאָחָז 2Kgs 23:30 + ). 10. a post-exilic prince of the line of David 1Chr 3:24 . 11. father of Azariah, priest in Solomon's time 1Chr 5:35 ; 1Chr 5:36 . 12. two of David's mighty men: \\ \\ a. a Benjamite 1Chr 12:5 \\ \\ b. a Gadite 1Chr 12:13 . 13. a returning exile Ezra 8:12 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2106')\">BDB2106</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3076')\">H3076</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H3110')\">H3110</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2105')\">BDB2105</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2107')\">BDB2107</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>יְהוֺחָנָן</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>יוֺחָנָן</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine</b> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> mostly <grk>Ἰωαναν</grk>, <grk>Ἰωναν</grk> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>י</bdbheb> <highlight>hath been gracious</highlight>, compare <bdbheb>אֶלְחָנָן</bdbheb> <bdbheb>חֲנַנְאֵל</bdbheb> &amp; references; also Phoenician <bdbheb>יחנבעל בעליחן</bdbheb>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>1. a.</b> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>יְהוֺ</bdbheb> a priest <ref ref=\"Neh 12:13\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(16,12,13)\">Neh 12:13</ref> <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> high priest <ref ref=\"Ezra 10:6\" b=\"15\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(15,10,6)\">Ezra 10:6</ref> = <bdbheb>יוֺחָנָן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Neh 12:22\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(16,12,22)\">Neh 12:22</ref>; <ref ref=\"Neh 12:23\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(16,12,23)\">Neh 12:23</ref> apparently = <bdbheb>יוֺנָתָן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Neh 12:11\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(16,12,11)\">Neh 12:11</ref> (twice in verse) (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Ἰωναθαν</grk>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>יְהוֺ</bdbheb> Levite <ref ref=\"Neh 12:42\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"42\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"42\" onclick=\"bcv(16,12,42)\">Neh 12:42</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>3.</b> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>יְהוֺ</bdbheb> son of Tobiah <ref ref=\"Neh 6:18\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(16,6,18)\">Neh 6:18</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> Manuscripts <grk>Ἰωναθαν</grk>). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>4.</b> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>יְהוֺ</bdbheb> porter in David's time <ref ref=\"1Chr 26:3\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(13,26,3)\">1Chr 26:3</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <grk>Ἰωνας</grk>